    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "THE\nSATURDAY\nEVENING\nPOST\nSUPER\n7\nPA-A\nCAN\nW\nAIRWAYS\nFLIGHT 62\nto PARIS\nano\nROME\nPAA\nPAN ANDRICAN SAID BASAnO\nOnly Pan American has crossed the Atlantic more than 50,000 times!\nIt's nice to know \"Uncle Sam's\" your skipper\nwhen you fly to faraway places\nNo country in the world has requirements of airline\noperation more strict than those of the U.S. Government.\nAnd when you fly Pan Am, it's reassuring to know that Uncle Sam's\nrules are met with a generous margin to spare by the only U.S.\nairline serving 78 countries and colonies around the world.\nPAN AMERICAN\nWORLD'S MOST EXPERIENCED AIRLINE"
    ],
